prs.body:
Computed TypeScript method keys must resolve in the enclosing scope. In:

```
declare const x: unique symbol;
interface I {
  [x](x: number): void;
}
```
The key currently binds to the parameter `x`; this change binds it to the outer constant.

Fix printing a negative `BigIntLiteral` after `-`.

```javascript
// Original
x = -(-1n);
// Printed - syntax error
x = --1n;
```

This bug could not be produced by an AST which has come from parser, because parser would parse the input as equivalent to `x = -(-(1n));`. But it could be produced when printing a hand-built AST.

Same fix as #27377, but for Rust `oxc_codegen`.

Unlike the JS codegen, incorrect output could be generated without manual AST manipulation - the minifier also produces such an AST in some cases.

```javascript
// Input
x = -~0n;
x = y - ~1n;
```

```javascript
// Minified output before this PR
x=--1n,x=y--2n;
```

